# arcint-flashnext — Qwen3.8-Flash-Next from the IQ3_S GGUF on the 24 GB card, on demand. The default
# since 2026-10-15 (operator). IQ2_XS, faster and less exact, runs from this unit with its file as --gguf and
# --llama-expert-cache 13400 (docs/llama-engine.md, "Flash-Next quant options").
#
# The IQ3_XXS quant option's quality step over IQ2_XS: KL 0.218 against unsloth's Q8_0 (IQ2_XS 0.294),
# top-1 89.7 % (87.1 %) (docs/llama-engine.md, "Flash-Next quant options"). The slot budget is 11,600 MiB,
# not IQ2_XS's 13,400: at 13,400 the card thrashed (peak 24,440 MiB, 6.4-11.7 t/s, from the ZFS pool).
#
# Measured on the Arc Pro B60 with the IQ3_XXS quant option and these flags (arcint 321fc1d, the file on the NVMe, 2026-10-15):
# - the 20,045-token needle read at 597.9 t/s and answered; Paris;
# - six answers (Strata's request, a hash table, a compiler, Python, German, a story) at 33.9 / 37.5 /
#   37.3 / 33.5 / 30.6 / 30.9 t/s with the CPU misses, against 20.7 / 26.2 / 28.9 / 18.7 / 21.2 / 18.5
#   without them (+52 % on the mean), 80-90 % of the routed experts on the card;
# - KL against unsloth's Q8_0 (8 x 512, ubatch 4) 0.290954 / top-1 86.618 % with the misses, 0.286562 /
#   86.765 % without (+0.0044 nats, inside the answer-level bar);
# - peak VRAM 23,306 MiB of 24,480, GTT 29,573 MiB (the bank); nothing evicted.
#
# The CPU misses on this file need 0056 as of 0.8.0: before it, the slow path read the IQ4_NL banks of
# 18 layers wrong and the first request faulted (contrib/llama.cpp/README.md, 0056).
#
# The GGUF and the draft head must be on local NVMe: from the ZFS pool an answer reads ~1 GB of experts
# from storage.
#
# prefill-slot-loan (2026-10-30; docs/campaigns/prefill-slot-loan.md, the design beside it):
# `--prefill-chunk 8192 --llama-slot-loan 6400 --llama-loan-chunk 8192` lend the cache's tail slots to a
# prompt's 8,192-token ubatch and refill them before decode. Measured on the card with an 11,600 MiB slot
# budget: the served-shape KL at the answer-level bar (-0.0030 nats, +1.79 points against the twin), the
# depth prefill 340.5 against 217.9 t/s (+56 %) at 103,638 tokens, the refill 0.539 s, 0 of 12,250 rows
# differing. **The three loan flags in this example unit are opt-in**: drop them and the unit serves the
# resident 2,048 chunk with no loan, as before.
#
# The sizing rule (rounds 21-25, design sections 26-32). At the loan's begin and at every growth step the
# kernel's device-wide figure decides: DRM_XE_DEVICE_QUERY_MEM_REGIONS on the process's xe render fd gives
# each VRAM region's used/total, and the rule is `used - lend + need + first_touch + allowance <= total`
# with the operator's zero margin beyond that `used` (it already holds every other client and the kernel's
# objects; `used - fdinfo` is logged as information, never a term). The process's own figure is the SUM of
# `drm-resident-vram0` and `drm-resident-gtt` over the distinct `drm-client-id`s whose `drm-pdev` is the
# device's (the OpenCL runtime opens two xe clients per card in one process); the ggml buffer sum is the
# fallback when the query fails and the tripwire (the summed vram0 below it means the process's buffers
# are evicted to GTT, the loan is refused). The only addend beside `need` and the cold stream ring's first
# touch is an optional prefill-growth allowance, default 0 (`LLAMA_SLOT_LOAN_PREFILL_GROWTH_MIB`). The
# 384 MiB peak reserve over `lend - need` stays as the reserve's own sanity. The lend grows one tail layer
# at a time until both rules hold, keeping the 8,192 chunk and the depth gain; a grown layer's lend bank
# is read from the file once per process. Round 25 makes the growth two-step: first the demand (need plus
# the carried shortfall), then, when the tail cannot reach it, the tail's full growth if it still meets
# `need` alone -- so a short tail costs one WARN and never refuses a loan the `need` rule allows.
#
# The eviction guard (rounds 22-23) takes the process's fdinfo GTT as its baseline at the begin and at the
# end judges the GTT growth since it (logged, never acted on) and the VRAM shortfall against the expected
# residency; only a TRUE shortfall (64 MiB floor, `LLAMA_SLOT_LOAN_SHED_FLOOR_MIB`) feeds the NEXT lend's
# sizing as growth -- never a shed, never a refusal -- and a clean loan clears it.
# `LLAMA_SLOT_LOAN_EVICTION_GUARD=0` turns the guard off. The `loan out` line prints the kernel used, the
# card's total, fdinfo vram0 and gtt, the ggml sum, `need`, the lend, the first touch, the allowance and
# the inequality; the campaign's owed window reads them against its 2 s sampler. The rule and its price
# are design sections 24b/24c and 26-32.

[Unit]
Description=arcint-flashnext — Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ3_S on libllama, expert cache + MTP, GPU.0, :8089
Documentation=https://github.com/marfrit/arcint
After=default.target
Conflicts=arcint-agent.service arcint-writer.service

[Service]
Type=simple
Environment=GGML_OPENCL_BANK_STREAM=1
Environment=LLAMA_EXPERT_CACHE_CPU_MISSES=1
ExecStart=/usr/bin/arcint \
    --engine llama \
    --gguf /flash-model/gguf-iq3s/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-IQ3_S-00001-of-00002.gguf \
    --served-model-name qwen3.8-flash-next \
    --device GPU.0 \
    --host 0.0.0.0 \
    --port 8089 \
    --n-ctx 131072 \
    --llama-cpu-moe 48 \
    --llama-threads 8 \
    --llama-expert-cache 11600 \
    --llama-kv q8_0 \
    --llama-expert-profile %h/.local/share/arcint/expert-profile-strata.bin \
    --llama-mtp 3 \
    --llama-mtp-min-p 0.5 \
    --llama-reserve-cells 20480 \
    --prefill-chunk 8192 \
    --llama-slot-loan 6400 \
    --llama-loan-chunk 8192 \
    --llama-mtp-gguf /models/gguf/fn-mtp/mtp-flash-next-q8e4n-hq4k.gguf \
    --queue-timeout 30
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=30
TimeoutStartSec=30min
TimeoutStopSec=90s
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=false
ProtectHome=read-only

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
